WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.302
Effective Articulate 360 course creation starts with instructional purpose,

00:00:03.302 --> 00:00:04.369
not tool exploration.

00:00:04.369 --> 00:00:08.995
Before choosing screens or interactions, define the learner, the performance goal, the scope,

00:00:08.995 --> 00:00:10.418
and the completion requirement.

00:00:10.418 --> 00:00:14.687
A course becomes easier to build and review when everyone agrees on

00:00:14.687 --> 00:00:18.245
what learners should be able to do after completing it.

00:00:18.245 --> 00:00:21.447
Strong courses combine clear objectives, structured content, useful narration,

00:00:21.447 --> 00:00:23.938
purposeful media, meaningful interactions, aligned assessment, accessibility,

00:00:23.938 --> 00:00:25.717
stakeholder review, and quality assurance.

00:00:25.717 --> 00:00:29.986
None of these pieces need to be complicated, but each one matters.

00:00:29.986 --> 00:00:32.833
Weak planning can make a beautiful course ineffective.

00:00:32.833 --> 00:00:36.391
Strong planning can make a simple course practical and memorable.

00:00:36.391 --> 00:00:39.237
The goal is not to use every feature.

00:00:39.237 --> 00:00:44.218
The goal is to build a learning experience that learners can understand, complete, apply,

00:00:44.218 --> 00:00:45.641
and revisit when needed.

00:00:45.641 --> 00:00:48.843
Rapid responsive courses may be ideal for some projects.

00:00:48.843 --> 00:00:52.045
Custom slide-based courses may be better for simulations, branching,

00:00:52.045 --> 00:00:53.113
or specialized interactions.

00:00:53.113 --> 00:00:55.959
The best choice depends on the learning problem.

00:00:55.959 --> 00:00:58.094
A durable course is also maintainable.

00:00:58.094 --> 00:01:01.652
Keep narration, media, source files, comments, and publishing settings organized.

00:01:01.652 --> 00:01:04.142
Check accessibility and LMS behavior before release.

00:01:04.142 --> 00:01:08.056
Use review feedback to improve clarity instead of simply collecting approvals.

00:01:08.056 --> 00:01:10.902
When the design stays focused on learner needs,

00:01:10.902 --> 00:01:14.816
the authoring tool becomes a practical means to an instructional end.

00:01:14.816 --> 00:01:18.374
The practical takeaway is simple: design decisions should be explainable.

00:01:18.374 --> 00:01:21.576
If a module exists, it should support an objective.

00:01:21.576 --> 00:01:24.778
If media is used, it should clarify or reinforce.

00:01:24.778 --> 00:01:29.047
If an interaction is included, it should create useful thinking or practice.

00:01:29.047 --> 00:01:30.826
If a quiz question appears,

00:01:30.826 --> 00:01:34.740
it should measure something the learner was actually expected to learn.
